This is where the EPICS CAD support files are located.  All of the files in this
 directory are compiled and linked into a single object file (epicsControl.o).  

The object file is loaded into vxworks before iocInit. 

Loading procedure
After the iocInit is run, initTasks must be run, which starts up all the control 
tasks. These tasks enter a while loop and then wait for a semaphore to be given
to them.  A corresponding cad routine releases the semaphore which allows a particular
control task to continue.    The cad routine starts the control task 
and returns before the task is finished.  If any errors occur in the control task, 
the error gets reported to the supervising car record which then filters up to
the applyC car record. 
 
Cad Control
Most of the files in this area have a corresponding cad record. These all have the
form <name>Cad.c (cad routine) or <name>Ctrl.c (control routine).  The cad routines
contain the function that is called directly by the cad record.  It supports all of the
Epics directives (mark, preset, clear, start stop).  The input values to the cad record  
are checked in the preset directive, and copied to the output VAL fields in the start 
directive.  The start directive is where any further processing is performed for those 
cad records  that require any.  One action that must take place in the start directive
is setting the car to busy.  Higher level software use the car record to know when
a particular task is processing, and if there is an error.   
	
Any time consuming processing is performed utilizing the control routine.  The control 
routines are spawned in the 'initTasks' process, and then wait on a semaphore.  The cad 
routine releases the semaphore and returns.  The Control task performs the required task, 
and then loops around and waits on the semaphore again.  When a control task is being 
utilized, it should be the one that sets the car back to idle or error.  Otherwise, the 
cad routine will take care of this function.

The rest of the files have functions useful to many of 
the routines.  


epicsCAInt.c  - Contains functions for using EPICS channel access.

epicsCA.c  -  Functions which use channel access to set SAD database values.

epCommon.c  -  Functions for accessing local database values.

epicsGlobals.c  -  Global variable definitions.

initTasks.c - Starts up all of the Ctrl tasks

combCars - Specialized function for copying the worst error of many inputs to the output

compSad - increment the heartBeat value (currently not used)
